er lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Celeste Maloy (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Utah's 3rd District is a heavily Republican seat, and incumbent Celeste Maloy is seeking reelection after winning renomination. Kent Udell, the Democratic nominee, has run an active campaign centered on public lands, affordability, and energy issues, with several debates across the district in early October drawing wide local coverage.\n\nThe structural picture strongly favors Maloy: the district leans Republican by about 21 points, she has raised roughly thirty times more than Udell, and a September poll of likely voters showed her ahead 45 to 26. Prediction markets give Democrats only a one to four percent chance. The forecast expects Maloy to win comfortably, with the main uncertainty being turnout and how third-party candidates draw votes.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0155, "margin": -18.58}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0256, "margin": -18.6}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0177, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0181, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0129, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0141, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0181, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0196, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0119, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -18.4}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.016, "margin": -18.4}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0126, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0174, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.005, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0087, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0046, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0072, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0063, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0052, "margin": -19.0}]}